.page cat 1 concatenate files and print them

# SYNOPSIS
*cat* [*-nEu*] [_FILE_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`cat` copies each _FILE_ to standard output in order. With no file, or for the name `-`, it copies standard input. A file that cannot be opened is reported and the rest are still copied.

# OPTIONS
@ *-n*
    Number all output lines, starting at 1 and continuing across files. The number is right-aligned in six columns and followed by a tab.
@ *-E*
    Put a `$` at the end of each line, so trailing white space shows.
@ *-u*
    Accepted and ignored.

Options can be combined (`-nE`) and must come first.

# EXIT STATUS
0, 1 if a file could not be read, 2 for an unknown option.

# EXAMPLES
    cat /Hakurei/etc/hostname
    cat -n script.sh
    cat a.txt - b.txt > all.txt
    cat > note.txt

# SEE ALSO
tac(1), head(1), tail(1), patchouli-pager(1), pnote(1)
